WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.340
They met in the dissection hall at Prague and recognized each other at once as the

2
00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.480
same kind of person.

3
00:00:09.333 --> 00:00:15.033
They married, came to the United States in 1922, and ran headlong into the rules of

4
00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:19.653
the era: a Buffalo institute director ordered Gerty to stop publishing with her

5
00:00:19.653 --> 00:00:24.893
husband, and she refused; at Washington University she was hired at a tenth of

6
00:00:24.893 --> 00:00:28.013
Carl's salary for 16 years under nepotism rules.

7
00:00:28.933 --> 00:00:33.233
The lab she built at that salary trained five future Nobel laureates.

8
00:00:33.593 --> 00:00:37.933
Working through a fraction everyone else threw away the supernatant left from

9
00:00:37.933 --> 00:00:42.533
recrystallizing phosphorylase they found the debranching enzyme, and Gerty

10
00:00:42.533 --> 00:00:47.313
understood the chromatography spot instantly and ran down the hall shouting, "It's

11
00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:49.073
free glucose, it's free glucose!"

12
00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:54.673
She went further, matching the wrong-shaped glycogen in sick children to a specific

13
00:00:54.673 --> 00:00:59.713
missing enzyme: the first proof that one broken enzyme can cause an inherited

14
00:00:59.713 --> 00:01:00.713
disease.

15
00:01:01.117 --> 00:01:07.057
When the Nobel came in 1947, Carl said at the banquet that including his wife was "a

16
00:01:07.057 --> 00:01:09.037
source of deep satisfaction to me."

17
00:01:09.677 --> 00:01:12.157
He was not being gallant; he was being accurate.

18
00:01:12.817 --> 00:01:16.737
The same year, Washington University finally made Gerty a full professor.
